            <ArticleTitle>Modulatory impact of cardiac rehabilitation on hyperhomocysteinemia in patients with coronary artery disease and &quot;normal&quot; lipid levels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1543-5, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In coronary patients with &quot;relatively normal&quot; lipid values and hyperhomocystinemia (levels &gt; or =15 micromol/L), significant 12% reductions in homocysteine levels occurred after cardiac rehabilitation and exercise training. This benefit from cardiac rehabilitation and exercise training may lead to 20% to 30% reductions in overall coronary artery disease risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
